        "subject": "LU-12669 ptlrpc: fetch target statfs with the first ping",
        "message": "LU-12669 ptlrpc: fetch target statfs with the first ping\n\nA client only fetches the statfs data of an OST, or of an MDT other\nthan MDT0000, when something asks for it, such as \"lfs df\", so until\nthen the client does not know that the target is on flash\n(OS_STATFS_NONROT), e.g. to prefer a flash mirror of an FLR file for\nreads (lov_init_composite()).\n\nAny request from the client serves as a ping, so if the OSC or MDC\nimport of a client has no statfs data yet, send OST_STATFS or\nMDS_STATFS instead of OBD_PING and cache the reply in the OSC or MDC\nas obd_statfs() does.  Do this even if the import is idle by then,\nsince an unused import goes idle before its first ping.  Like a ping\nit is neither resent nor delayed, and it is tried once per connection,\nso a target that refuses it, e.g. to a client banned by nodemap, does\nnot keep the import from going idle.\n\nAlso cache the reply to the asynchronous statfs that LMV sends when an\nMDC connects (mdc_statfs_interpret()), so that every MDC has the\nstatfs data of its MDT from the start.\n\nAdd sanity test_812e to check that each OSC and MDC fetches the\nstatfs data of its target after a remount.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ic60238c1fc78328603205b285527676b093ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
